  "card": "Fixes an issue in the sendall RPC where supplying valid uppercase bech32 addresses without an amount fails with a dust threshold error. Previously, recipients without amounts were tracked as raw strings and compared against canonical lowercase address strings produced by EncodeDestination, failing to match uppercase inputs and leaving output amounts at zero. The change matches decoded destinations directly rather than raw address strings. A functional test demonstrates that sweeping to an uppercase address fails on master and succeeds with this patch.",
